Subject: [PATCH] base: constrain the signed-byte unaligned-read overload

Older Solaris headers typedef int8_t to char rather than signed char. The
char and int8_t overloads then have identical signatures, which breaks V8's
cppgc build. Keep the int8_t overload only for a distinct signed-byte type;
the existing char overload handles the legacy typedef without ambiguity.

Constrain the deduced type to int8_t so unrelated pointer types do not gain
an unaligned-read overload. No integer typedef or ABI changes are needed.

--- a/v8-152.2.0/v8/src/base/memory.h
+++ b/v8-152.2.0/v8/src/base/memory.h
@@ -37,8 +37,9 @@
   return ReadUnalignedValue<V>(reinterpret_cast<Address>(p));
 }
 
-template <typename V>
-static inline V ReadUnalignedValue(const int8_t p[sizeof(V)]) {
+template <typename V, typename Byte>
+  requires(std::is_same_v<Byte, int8_t> && !std::is_same_v<Byte, char>)
+static inline V ReadUnalignedValue(const Byte p[sizeof(V)]) {
   return ReadUnalignedValue<V>(reinterpret_cast<Address>(p));
 }
 
